One potential solution is to use a smaller version of the DistilBERT model, such as DistilBERT-base-uncased, which might have fewer parameters and thus require less memory. Another approach is to use a CPU-based solution, although this would be significantly slower.

Let's modify the script to use a smaller version of the DistilBERT model and see if this resolves the issue.

